{# Subscription tier — one deployment per registry entry, credential-gated.
   Split out of model-list.yaml.j2 when that file crossed its per-file token
   budget, following the seam that file already uses for the light tier and the
   Hermes agents: one tier per file, so an agent changing this tier reads this
   file and not every other tier as well. Per .token-limits.yaml the remedy for
   an over-budget file is a split along a real seam, never a raised budget.

   Included by model-list.yaml.j2, which owns the macros and the surrounding
   tiers; `delegation_hints` and `litellm_model` resolve from that context. #}
  # --- Subscription tier ---
  # Each entry renders exactly one deployment, under its own registry id. See
  # defaults/main/32-opencode.yml for what `order` does here, which today is
  # nothing: it ranks deployments within one model_name group, and no entry in
  # this tier shares a name with another tier's.
  #
  # x-opencode-session: OpenCode Zen/Go has rejected every request missing this
  # header since 2026-09-06 ("Request is missing x-opencode-session and cannot
  # be routed efficiently") — https://opencode.ai/docs/zen/. The vendor wants
  # "one stable ID per conversation", injected per request from the caller's
  # own session; litellm_params is rendered once at config load, so it cannot
  # carry a per-conversation value without a custom pre_call_hook (litellm
  # 1.102.0 has no built-in per-request header templating — router.py's
  # extra_headers handling, ~11773, only ever forwards the static config
  # value). A value stable PER DEPLOYMENT is the closest a static config can
  # get, and it still satisfies the one check that actually gates the
  # request: presence. ponytail: router-wide stability, not per-caller;
  # upgrade to real per-conversation ids with a pre_call_hook keyed on
  # metadata.session_id if OpenCode's cache-hit rate on this tier ever
  # matters enough to justify one.
{% for m in llm_router_opencode_models %}
{% set _oc_env = m.credential_env %}
{% set _oc_key = llm_router_resolved_credentials.get(_oc_env, '') %}
{% if _oc_key | length > 0 %}
  - model_name: {{ m.client_model_id }}
    litellm_params:
      model: {{ litellm_model(m) }}
      api_base: {{ m.api_base | default(llm_router_opencode_base_url) }}
      api_key: os.environ/{{ _oc_env }}
      use_chat_completions_api: true
      extra_headers:
        x-opencode-session: "hermes-router-{{ m.client_model_id | regex_replace('/', '-') }}"
      order: {{ m.order | default(llm_router_opencode_default_order) }}
      rpm: {{ m.rpm | default(llm_router_opencode_rpm) }}
      tpm: {{ m.tpm | default(llm_router_opencode_tpm) }}
      max_parallel_requests: {{ m.max_parallel_requests | default(llm_router_opencode_max_parallel_requests) }}
    model_info:
      max_input_tokens: {{ m.context_window }}
      max_output_tokens: {{ m.max_output_tokens }}
      max_tokens: {{ m.max_output_tokens }}
{{- delegation_hints(m) }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
